From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:14:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Answer GetRuntimeClassName on activation factories as
 WRL does.

Windows's are WRL activation factories, which are no runtime class and
return E_ILLEGAL_METHOD_CALL, leaving the name alone; winref (Windows 11
build 29671) answers so for CompositionEffectSourceParameter's.  The
effect factory's LoadStatus is still Pending right after it is made
there, so the test takes either.  The tracker tests trace the states a
custom animation past the bounds and an inertia go through, instead of
checking what Windows does otherwise: it lets the animation past the
bounds and coasts back, and reports a modified resting position always.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/controller.c b/dlls/dcomp/controller.c
index 1ec07c41fba..1bc62c77ee8 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/controller.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/controller.c
@@ -444,10 +444,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI factory_GetIids( IActivationFactory *iface, ULONG *iid_cou
     return E_NOTIMPL;
 }
 
+/* an activation factory is no runtime class: WRL's, which Windows's are, say so */
 static HRESULT WINAPI factory_GetRuntimeClassName( IActivationFactory *iface, HSTRING *class_name )
 {
-    FIXME( "iface %p, class_name %p stub!\n", iface, class_name );
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+    TRACE( "iface %p, class_name %p.\n", iface, class_name );
+    return E_ILLEGAL_METHOD_CALL;
 }
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI factory_GetTrustLevel( IActivationFactory *iface, TrustLevel *trust_level )
